1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:04,540
You're here.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,380
Your organs are failing.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,300
And your death is drawing near.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,440
But if you bribe the right politicians in the right order at the right time,

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,600
you can trade the nuclear warheads for medicine.

6
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,080
And it's not even a crime.

7
00:01:40,284 --> 00:01:41,364
Health Dividend

8
00:01:42,304 --> 00:01:47,244
Six thousand six hundred and fifty diseases have zero approved treatments.

9
00:01:47,984 --> 00:01:52,044
At your current pace, you'll get to all of them in four hundred and forty-three

10
00:01:52,044 --> 00:01:52,544
years.

11
00:01:53,804 --> 00:01:58,324
Redirect one percent of military spending and it drops to thirty-six years,

12
00:01:59,004 --> 00:02:03,884
preventing ten point seven billion deaths at nine thousand two hundred times

13
00:02:03,884 --> 00:02:06,644
the cost-effectiveness of anti-malaria bed nets.

14
00:02:07,424 --> 00:02:11,564
The whole thing costs less per year to run than Halloween costumes for dogs.

15
00:02:12,103 --> 00:02:14,164
But sure, take your time.

16
00:02:14,904 --> 00:02:16,764
That was the peace dividend:

17
00:02:16,824 --> 00:02:20,124
the money you get from buying one percent fewer explosions.

18
00:02:20,744 --> 00:02:22,764
Now here is the health dividend:

19
00:02:23,284 --> 00:02:25,644
what happens when you spend it on medicine instead.

20
00:02:26,804 --> 00:02:31,424
Right now, somewhere in your regulatory system, a drug that already passed

21
00:02:31,424 --> 00:02:35,084
safety testing is sitting in a filing cabinet while the disease it treats

22
00:02:35,084 --> 00:02:36,424
keeps killing people.

23
00:02:37,124 --> 00:02:41,464
Somewhere else, a researcher with a promising compound for one of six thousand

24
00:02:41,464 --> 00:02:46,044
six hundred and fifty untreated diseases is filling out the same form for

25
00:02:46,044 --> 00:02:46,564
the fourth time.

26
00:02:47,904 --> 00:02:51,364
The health dividend is what happens when you stop doing this.

27
00:02:52,264 --> 00:02:56,344
It is worth seven point five three quadrillion dollars.

28
00:02:57,084 --> 00:02:58,634
That number is not a typo.

29
00:02:58,804 --> 00:02:59,304
I checked.

30
00:02:59,504 --> 00:03:00,304
Your economists checked.

31
00:03:00,764 --> 00:03:01,344
Everyone checked.

32
00:03:01,744 --> 00:03:02,664
It's still that number.

33
00:03:03,284 --> 00:03:05,004
The rest of this chapter is the receipt.

34
00:03:06,384 --> 00:03:08,284
From Explosions to Trial Slots.

35
00:03:09,504 --> 00:03:12,024
Twenty-seven point two billion dollars arrives from the peace dividend.

36
00:03:13,104 --> 00:03:16,524
Investor and political allocations take their cut, leaving twenty-one point

37
00:03:16,524 --> 00:03:19,724
eight billion dollars for medical research (eighty percent of the total).

38
00:03:20,664 --> 00:03:22,104
Your decentralized F.D.A.

39
00:03:22,104 --> 00:03:23,944
takes forty million dollars to keep the lights on.

40
00:03:24,724 --> 00:03:27,484
That leaves twenty-one point seven billion dollars for trial subsidies.

41
00:03:29,064 --> 00:03:31,184
I am now going to show you what that money buys.

42
00:03:31,684 --> 00:03:33,944
I apologize in advance for the number of numbers.

43
00:03:34,324 --> 00:03:38,224
Your species requires receipts before it will believe anything, even things

44
00:03:38,224 --> 00:03:39,584
that are obviously true.

45
00:03:40,424 --> 00:03:42,694
Especially things that are obviously true.

46
00:03:43,444 --> 00:03:46,564
Your current system charges forty-one thousand dollars per patient in a

47
00:03:46,564 --> 00:03:47,224
clinical trial.

48
00:03:47,844 --> 00:03:52,304
I asked why and was told "regulatory compliance, site management, and monitoring

49
00:03:52,304 --> 00:03:52,804
overhead,"

50
00:03:53,404 --> 00:03:57,184
which I believe is the human phrase for "permission costs more than medicine."

51
00:03:57,944 --> 00:04:01,564
Pragmatic trials, the kind your decentralized F.D.A.

52
00:04:01,564 --> 00:04:03,284
runs, cost nine hundred and twenty-nine dollars.

53
00:04:03,824 --> 00:04:04,324
At that price,

54
00:04:04,784 --> 00:04:08,444
twenty-one point seven billion dollars buys you twenty-three point four

55
00:04:08,444 --> 00:04:10,404
million trial slots per year.

56
00:04:11,104 --> 00:04:15,764
Your species currently enrolls one point nine million patients per year

57
00:04:15,764 --> 00:04:17,624
in clinical trials globally.

58
00:04:18,124 --> 00:04:22,024
The treaty adds twelve point three times more capacity on top of that.

59
00:04:22,684 --> 00:04:23,864
Remember this number.

60
00:04:24,244 --> 00:04:25,904
Everything that follows depends on it.

61
00:04:27,044 --> 00:04:27,944
The Waiting List.

62
00:04:28,944 --> 00:04:31,734
You met the queue in the untapped therapeutic frontier:

63
00:04:32,764 --> 00:04:36,784
six thousand six hundred and fifty diseases with zero approved treatments,

64
00:04:37,164 --> 00:04:39,704
and fifteen getting their first treatment per year.

65
00:04:40,204 --> 00:04:44,384
At that rate, you clear the backlog in four hundred and forty-three years.

66
00:04:45,144 --> 00:04:47,084
I will let you sit with that number for a moment.

67
00:04:47,624 --> 00:04:50,364
It is longer than your species has had writing.

68
00:04:51,304 --> 00:04:55,304
For context, four hundred and forty-three years ago, Shakespeare was writing

69
00:04:55,304 --> 00:05:00,204
plays, Galileo was building telescopes, and your species already had printing

70
00:05:00,204 --> 00:05:03,844
presses, universities, and intercontinental shipping.

71
00:05:03,864 --> 00:05:06,624
You just had not gotten around to curing most diseases.

72
00:05:07,244 --> 00:05:11,004
At this pace, you still will not for another four hundred and forty-three

73
00:05:11,004 --> 00:05:11,504
years.

74
00:05:12,124 --> 00:05:15,384
Apply the twelve point three times multiplier.

75
00:05:15,884 --> 00:05:19,744
Instead of fifteen diseases getting their first treatment per year, you

76
00:05:19,744 --> 00:05:23,084
get one hundred and eighty-five diseases per year.

77
00:05:23,504 --> 00:05:27,444
The queue clears in thirty-six years instead of four hundred and forty-three

78
00:05:27,444 --> 00:05:27,944
years.

79
00:05:28,364 --> 00:05:32,104
The average untreated disease gets its first treatment two hundred and four

80
00:05:32,104 --> 00:05:33,124
years earlier.

81
00:05:33,864 --> 00:05:37,304
That is the difference between "your grandchildren might see a cure" and

82
00:05:37,304 --> 00:05:38,604
"you might see a cure."

83
00:05:39,364 --> 00:05:42,024
Most observers consider this a meaningful distinction.

84
00:05:42,544 --> 00:05:46,284
On Earth, it apparently requires a seventy-eight-page chapter to justify.

85
00:05:47,164 --> 00:05:51,744
Your species figured out how to split atoms in six years during a war, but

86
00:05:51,744 --> 00:05:55,384
letting a cancer patient take a pill that passed safety testing requires

87
00:05:55,384 --> 00:05:58,284
the gestation period of three consecutive elephants.

88
00:05:58,904 --> 00:06:02,404
The twelve point three times multiplier compresses the elephant parade.

89
00:06:03,204 --> 00:06:05,324
But trial capacity is only half the delay.

90
00:06:05,844 --> 00:06:09,724
Once a drug passes safety testing, your regulatory system sits on it for

91
00:06:09,724 --> 00:06:13,844
another eight point two years to confirm it works well enough, while people

92
00:06:13,844 --> 00:06:15,784
who could be taking it die instead.

93
00:06:16,564 --> 00:06:19,284
Add the capacity acceleration and the efficacy lag together:

94
00:06:20,324 --> 00:06:24,204
two hundred and twelve years of dying, condensed into not dying.

95
00:06:24,964 --> 00:06:27,044
The Body Count.

96
00:06:27,144 --> 00:06:30,204
one hundred and fifty thousand people die from disease every day.

97
00:06:30,784 --> 00:06:34,184
While you were reading the previous section, approximately three hundred

98
00:06:34,184 --> 00:06:34,764
of them did.

99
00:06:35,244 --> 00:06:37,504
They are not coming back to find out how the math turned out.

100
00:06:38,324 --> 00:06:41,704
Not all of those deaths are currently preventable, but ninety-two point

101
00:06:41,704 --> 00:06:46,394
six percent are *eventually* avoidable with sufficient biomedical research.

102
00:06:46,604 --> 00:06:49,764
"Eventually avoidable" does not mean "currently preventable."

103
00:06:50,184 --> 00:06:50,684
It means:

104
00:06:50,944 --> 00:06:54,284
given enough research, these diseases have biological solutions.

105
00:06:55,144 --> 00:06:58,704
The only category excluded is accidents (falling off things, being hit by

106
00:06:58,704 --> 00:06:59,204
things).

107
00:06:59,824 --> 00:07:03,964
Every disease, including aging, is a biological process, and biological

108
00:07:03,964 --> 00:07:06,564
processes are, in principle, fixable.

109
00:07:07,364 --> 00:07:10,164
This is the theoretical ceiling, not a near-term promise.

110
00:07:11,224 --> 00:07:15,624
Over a two hundred and twelve-year timeline shift, the cumulative toll:

111
00:07:16,264 --> 00:07:18,524
ten point seven billion deaths.

112
00:07:19,064 --> 00:07:23,464
That is five hundred and sixty-five billion disability-adjusted life years,

113
00:07:23,524 --> 00:07:28,784
or D.A.L.Y.s of healthy life, and one point nine three quadrillion hours

114
00:07:28,784 --> 00:07:30,224
of suffering eliminated.

115
00:07:31,124 --> 00:07:35,544
These are cumulative, one-time benefits from permanently accelerating the

116
00:07:35,544 --> 00:07:40,084
discovery pipeline, the same methodology used to value smallpox eradication.

117
00:07:41,084 --> 00:07:43,904
Nobody objected to the methodology when it was used for smallpox.

118
00:07:44,724 --> 00:07:48,664
They will object now because the number is larger, which is a strange reason

119
00:07:48,664 --> 00:07:50,504
to object to saving more people.

120
00:07:51,184 --> 00:07:53,384
The Price Tag on Not Being Dead.

121
00:07:54,244 --> 00:07:57,444
Your governments already put a price on human life when deciding whether

122
00:07:57,444 --> 00:07:59,044
to approve drugs, build highways,

123
00:07:59,724 --> 00:08:00,664
or regulate pollution.

124
00:08:01,084 --> 00:08:01,944
The standard rate:

125
00:08:02,524 --> 00:08:05,864
one hundred and fifty thousand dollars per quality-adjusted life year.

126
00:08:06,784 --> 00:08:10,444
Your species finds this uncomfortable to discuss but does it constantly.

127
00:08:11,044 --> 00:08:13,844
You just prefer to do it in footnotes, where the dying can't see.

128
00:08:14,724 --> 00:08:18,504
The world loses two point eight eight billion D.A.L.Y.s per year.

129
00:08:19,084 --> 00:08:22,544
ninety-two point six percent are *eventually* avoidable with sufficient

130
00:08:22,544 --> 00:08:23,044
research.

131
00:08:23,764 --> 00:08:26,424
At one hundred and fifty thousand dollars per Q.A.L.Y.,

132
00:08:27,084 --> 00:08:30,424
that is four hundred trillion dollars per year in welfare losses.

133
00:08:31,264 --> 00:08:34,544
Multiply by the two hundred and twelve-year timeline shift and you get the

134
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:36,744
total economic value of the health dividend:

135
00:08:37,604 --> 00:08:40,204
seven point five three quadrillion dollars.

136
00:08:40,784 --> 00:08:43,324
"But that is more than global G.D.P.!"

137
00:08:43,784 --> 00:08:44,704
Yes.

138
00:08:44,924 --> 00:08:45,424
G.D.P.

139
00:08:45,724 --> 00:08:49,744
(one hundred and fifteen trillion dollars) measures market transactions.

140
00:08:50,244 --> 00:08:54,684
It does not measure the value of not being dead, not being in pain, and

141
00:08:54,684 --> 00:08:57,544
not watching your children die of treatable diseases.

142
00:08:58,284 --> 00:09:02,104
The one hundred and fifty thousand dollars per quality-adjusted life year,

143
00:09:02,384 --> 00:09:05,904
or Q.A.L.Y., figure is not something I invented.

144
00:09:06,344 --> 00:09:09,884
I just multiplied it by the number of sick people, which is also not my

145
00:09:09,884 --> 00:09:10,384
fault.

146
00:09:10,884 --> 00:09:15,404
The only debatable input is whether the timeline shift is really approximately

147
00:09:15,404 --> 00:09:17,184
two hundred and twelve years.

148
00:09:17,724 --> 00:09:20,034
See the full derivation for how that number is calculated,

149
00:09:20,644 --> 00:09:24,004
and the Monte Carlo simulations for what happens when every input varies.

150
00:09:24,904 --> 00:09:26,524
The Receipt.

151
00:09:26,524 --> 00:09:28,084
Your decentralized F.D.A.

152
00:09:28,124 --> 00:09:30,424
costs forty million dollars per year to operate.

153
00:09:30,984 --> 00:09:35,044
For reference, this is roughly what your species spends annually on Halloween

154
00:09:35,044 --> 00:09:36,204
costumes for dogs.

155
00:09:36,904 --> 00:09:37,924
Less than one fighter jet.

156
00:09:38,924 --> 00:09:43,084
Less than what FIFA spends on "hospitality" (your word for bribing officials

157
00:09:43,084 --> 00:09:43,884
in a building with chandeliers).

158
00:09:45,344 --> 00:09:49,664
A system that could test cures for seven thousand diseases costs less to

159
00:09:49,704 --> 00:09:52,944
run than the outfits you put on animals that do not want to wear them.

160
00:09:54,024 --> 00:09:57,684
The R and D savings alone are forty point five billion dollars per year,

161
00:09:58,104 --> 00:10:02,064
a four hundred and thirty-nine to one return without counting a single human

162
00:10:02,064 --> 00:10:02,564
life.

163
00:10:03,324 --> 00:10:06,204
Include the lives (which you would think someone would, but your species

164
00:10:06,204 --> 00:10:08,854
has a long history of not counting the people who die quietly),

165
00:10:09,664 --> 00:10:13,964
and the treaty's total societal return hits seven point five three million

166
00:10:13,964 --> 00:10:14,584
to one.

167
00:10:15,543 --> 00:10:17,403
The cost per year of healthy life saved:

168
00:10:18,324 --> 00:10:19,643
nine dollars and sixty-two cents.

169
00:10:20,744 --> 00:10:24,424
Anti-malaria bed nets, the gold standard of cost-effective interventions,

170
00:10:24,944 --> 00:10:28,384
cost one hundred and eighty-four dollars per disability-adjusted life year,

171
00:10:28,604 --> 00:10:29,104
or D.A.L.Y.

172
00:10:30,204 --> 00:10:34,434
This system operates at nine thousand two hundred times the cost-effectiveness,

173
00:10:34,904 --> 00:10:36,344
at vastly greater scale.

174
00:10:37,184 --> 00:10:40,604
This costs less per life-year than mosquito nets and nobody has heard of

175
00:10:40,604 --> 00:10:41,324
it.

176
00:10:41,664 --> 00:10:45,384
Your species has spent more money marketing energy drinks.

177
00:10:45,984 --> 00:10:47,364
The total campaign investment:

178
00:10:48,064 --> 00:10:49,104
one billion dollars.

179
00:10:49,904 --> 00:10:53,384
Even the worst case (everything goes wrong, adoption is terrible,

180
00:10:54,024 --> 00:10:55,284
the servers catch fire)

181
00:10:55,944 --> 00:10:58,684
still returns an estimated sixty-six to one.

182
00:10:59,204 --> 00:11:03,264
Your worst medical outcome is better than your best military one.

183
00:11:04,284 --> 00:11:08,024
Every day without this system costs one hundred and eleven million dollars

184
00:11:08,024 --> 00:11:10,504
in wasted trial spending alone.

185
00:11:11,084 --> 00:11:13,584
The regulatory lag is not a safety feature.

186
00:11:13,924 --> 00:11:16,474
It is a waiting room where people die.

187
00:11:16,724 --> 00:11:17,964
You just gave it a nicer name.

188
00:11:19,144 --> 00:11:20,524
For you personally:

189
00:11:20,524 --> 00:11:24,884
if diseases get cured even a few years earlier, the average human gains

190
00:11:25,224 --> 00:11:29,684
roughly fifty thousand extra hours of life and five hundred and eighteen

191
00:11:29,684 --> 00:11:34,144
thousand eight hundred and seventy-nine dollars in additional lifetime income

192
00:11:35,164 --> 00:11:39,184
(the treaty path multiplies cumulative earnings by one point five seven

193
00:11:39,184 --> 00:11:39,684
times).

194
00:11:40,504 --> 00:11:42,644
You spent seventeen minutes reading this chapter.

195
00:11:43,324 --> 00:11:46,584
That is a one hundred and seventy-six thousand times return on your time

196
00:11:46,584 --> 00:11:50,544
and a per-minute income gain that makes your day job look decorative.

197
00:11:51,644 --> 00:11:53,724
Your best investment ever was reading.

198
00:11:54,084 --> 00:11:57,944
I realize the irony, given that most of you stopped reading twelve paragraphs

199
00:11:57,944 --> 00:11:58,484
ago.

200
00:11:59,504 --> 00:12:02,384
See impact dot war on disease dot O.R.G.

201
00:12:02,444 --> 00:12:07,020
for derivations, Monte Carlo simulations, and the comparative cost-effectiveness table.

202
00:12:07,020 --> 00:12:12,560
Thank you so much for taking the time to end war and disease, but if at

203
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:16,780
any point you decide you're too busy, please press the share button on your

204
00:12:16,780 --> 00:12:20,480
glowing rectangle in case one of your friends have a free afternoon to end

205
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:21,520
war and disease instead.

206
00:12:22,140 --> 00:12:26,480
And if you're too busy to even do that, please leave a really, really, really

207
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:30,640
good rating and review so we overcome the pro -war algorithmic suppression

208
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:34,200
and find someone with more spare time for ending wars and diseases.

209
00:12:34,760 --> 00:12:36,960
The good review doesn't have to be true, they don't check.

210
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:41,560
But if you're too busy to even do that, the absolute least you could do

211
00:12:41,560 --> 00:12:47,180
is take 15 seconds to go to WarOnDisease.org and make your wishocratic allocation,

212
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:51,160
telling us what fraction of humanity's resources should go to explosions

213
00:12:51,160 --> 00:12:52,620
versus clinical trials.

214
00:12:52,900 --> 00:12:53,400
And vote!

215
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:58,080
If the 1% treaty passes, your vote will be personally to blame for saving

216
00:12:58,080 --> 00:13:02,700
2.6 lives and preventing 468,000 hours of suffering.

217
00:13:02,700 --> 00:13:05,400
Go to WarOnDisease.org right now.

218
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:06,360
Love you, bye!
